WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.665
The secret garden bloomed and bloomed, and every day revealed new miracles.

2
00:00:07.666 --> 00:00:10.588
There were eggs in the robin's nest.

3
00:00:10.589 --> 00:00:14.248
The robin's mate sat upon them until they hatched.

4
00:00:14.249 --> 00:00:18.754
On sunny days the robin watched the children working in the garden.

5
00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:25.439
But on rainy days the robin and his family had the garden to themselves.

6
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.633
One morning when the rain was streaming down, Colin was lying on his sofa.

7
00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:36.692
"Now that I'm a real boy, my arms and legs are so full of magic that I can't keep them still.

8
00:00:36.693 --> 00:00:39.763
They want to be doing things all the time.

9
00:00:39.764 --> 00:00:42.890
But it's not safe to get up and walk about.

10
00:00:42.891 --> 00:00:46.068
What do you think would happen if I did that?"

11
00:00:46.069 --> 00:00:51.675
Mary laughed. "The nurse and Mrs. Medlock would come running.

12
00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:54.723
They'd send for Dr. Craven for sure."

13
00:00:54.724 --> 00:00:57.355
"I wish my father would come home.

14
00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:01.449
I don't know how much longer I can go on pretending I'm not well.

15
00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.692
I wish it wasn't raining."

16
00:01:03.693 --> 00:01:06.870
It was then that Mary had an idea.

17
00:01:06.871 --> 00:01:10.385
"Do you know how many rooms are in this house?"

18
00:01:10.386 --> 00:01:13.232
Colin guessed about a thousand.

19
00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:16.740
"There are at least a hundred that no one goes into.

20
00:01:16.741 --> 00:01:20.809
I could push you in your wheelchair, and we could visit some of them."

21
00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.933
Colin liked that idea.

22
00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:29.052
When they reached the long picture gallery, he sprang from his wheelchair.

23
00:01:29.053 --> 00:01:33.866
"I am going to run from one end of the gallery to the other," he said.

24
00:01:33.867 --> 00:01:37.052
They ran up and down the gallery.

25
00:01:37.053 --> 00:01:41.353
Then they did some strengthening exercises that Dickon had taught them.

26
00:01:41.354 --> 00:01:46.631
After that they wandered through the house opening doors.

27
00:01:46.632 --> 00:01:51.229
They came upon the picture of the girl in the green dress.

28
00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.801
"She looks a bit like you, Mary," said Colin.

29
00:01:54.802 --> 00:01:58.833
"Not as you look now, but as you looked when you first came here.

30
00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:02.161
Now you are a great deal fatter and better looking."

31
00:02:02.162 --> 00:02:09.110
"So are you," said Mary, and they both laughed.

32
00:02:09.111 --> 00:02:13.663
Eventually they came back to Colin's room for lunch.

33
00:02:13.664 --> 00:02:19.713
Mary wanted to ask him a question because for several days she'd noticed a change in the room.

34
00:02:19.714 --> 00:02:24.160
The curtain was drawn back to reveal the picture of Colin's mother.

35
00:02:24.161 --> 00:02:30.428
"Two nights ago there was so much moonlight in the room, I woke up," Colin explained.

36
00:02:30.429 --> 00:02:35.242
"A patch of moonlight was shining on the curtain, so I pulled the cord to open it.

37
00:02:35.243 --> 00:02:40.618
My mother was looking right down at me and laughing, as if she were glad to see me standing there.

38
00:02:40.619 --> 00:02:43.418
I want to see her all the time now.

39
00:02:43.419 --> 00:02:47.427
I think she must have been some sort of magic person."

40
00:02:47.428 --> 00:02:51.653
"Sometimes I think you are her ghost made into a boy."

41
00:02:51.654 --> 00:02:55.503
"If I were her ghost, my father would be fond of me.

42
00:02:55.504 --> 00:02:59.922
Then I could tell him about the magic, and that would make him more cheerful."

43
00:02:59.923 --> 00:03:03.634
"That would be wonderful," said Mary.

44
00:03:03.635 --> 00:03:08.685
The next day the weather cleared, and the children were able to go out into the garden.

45
00:03:08.686 --> 00:03:12.618
Dickon and Mary were busy weeding when Colin called to them.

46
00:03:12.619 --> 00:03:15.856
"Mary! Dickon! Look at me!"

47
00:03:15.857 --> 00:03:19.830
They stopped working and looked at him, standing there.

48
00:03:19.831 --> 00:03:23.157
"Do you remember that first morning you brought me here?

49
00:03:23.158 --> 00:03:27.021
I was just thinking about that as I was digging with my trowel.

50
00:03:27.022 --> 00:03:32.027
So I had to stand up on my feet once more, to make sure I could really do it.

51
00:03:32.028 --> 00:03:36.205
And it is real! I'm well! I'm well!

52
00:03:36.206 --> 00:03:39.420
And I'm going to live forever and ever!"

53
00:03:39.421 --> 00:03:43.904
"Let's sing a song to celebrate," said Mary.

54
00:03:43.905 --> 00:03:46.858
They stood together and sang a hymn.

55
00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:51.837
As the last notes died away, Colin suddenly noticed something.

56
00:03:51.838 --> 00:03:55.736
"Someone's coming!" He pointed toward the door in the wall.

57
00:03:55.737 --> 00:03:59.263
A woman was entering the secret garden.

58
00:03:59.264 --> 00:04:03.179
Colin had never seen her before, but he wasn't afraid.

59
00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.992
Somehow he felt as if he already knew her.

60
00:04:06.993 --> 00:04:09.793
"It's Mother—that's who it is!"

61
00:04:09.794 --> 00:04:13.638
Dickon ran across the grass toward the kind-looking woman.

62
00:04:13.639 --> 00:04:16.850
He brought his mother over to Mary and Colin.

63
00:04:16.851 --> 00:04:20.547
"I told her where the door is because I knew you wanted to meet her."

64
00:04:20.548 --> 00:04:25.309
"Even when I was ill, I wanted to see you." Colin shook her hand.

65
00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:28.214
"You and Dickon and the secret garden.

66
00:04:28.215 --> 00:04:31.953
I'd never wanted to see anyone or anything before."

67
00:04:31.954 --> 00:04:37.537
"Oh, my dear boy." Tears filled Susan Sowerby's eyes.

68
00:04:37.538 --> 00:04:41.585
"Are you surprised that I am so well?" asked Colin.

69
00:04:41.586 --> 00:04:44.374
She put her hand on his shoulder.

70
00:04:44.375 --> 00:04:51.196
"Yes, I am, but you look so much like your mother that it makes my heart jump."

71
00:04:51.197 --> 00:04:57.071
Colin suddenly felt shy. "Do you think that will make my father like me?"

72
00:04:57.072 --> 00:05:01.149
"Oh, for sure." She patted his arm.

73
00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:05.499
"Your own dear mother is in this garden, I do believe.

74
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.989
She couldn't keep out of it.

75
00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:16.860
And now your father must come home to see the miracle blooming here."

